      "type": "callout",
      "from_line": 15,
      "to_line": 25,
      "title": "three ways to pass a value",
      "text": "takes(s) moves the String: main loses it. len(&s) borrows it read-only, so main keeps using t afterwards. push(&mut s) borrows it mutably: only one such borrow may exist at a time, and the caller sees the change.",
      "placement": "auto",
      "color": "cyan"
